  "label": "HVAC (heating and cooling)",
  "extends": "_shared",
  "_comment": "Back 2026-09-21 after being dropped on 2026-08-20. Residential HVAC firms are very often 'Plumbing, Heating & Air' shops that carry Plumber as a SECONDARY category, and the shared deny scans every category, so this trade escapes 'plumbing' and 'plumber' from deny; a firm Google files FIRST as a plumber is still refused by the inherited primary_deny. Air duct cleaning is the same shape: a common secondary on real installers, so it leaves recurring_deny here and is refused only as a primary. Drain, sewer, rooter and septic stay denied, as do filter delivery and maintenance-plan outfits. The generic installation-service and repair-service rules are restated with the HVAC forms added, which _shared stopped carrying when the trade was dropped.",
